WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.130
Your head teacher just showed me

2
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.190
a camera that takes the register

3
00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.730
by recognising faces.

4
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.540
It would save ten minutes a day.

5
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.690
Should your school buy it?

6
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.660
Today: who decides what’s fair, and

7
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.900
five questions to ask any AI.

8
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.750
Five questions fit any AI.

9
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.240
Is it fair: does it work for everyone?

10
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.400
Is it private: what data, and who sees it?

11
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.840
Is it open about how it decides?

12
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.460
Who answers for its mistakes?

13
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.240
And did the people it affects agree?

14
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.850
Behind every AI are people’s choices,

15
00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.250
like which mistake is worse.

16
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.120
If the camera marks a present student

17
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.380
absent, they may be in trouble at home.

18
00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.170
If it marks an absent one present,

19
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.110
nobody notices they’re missing.

20
00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:54.670
Which is worse?

21
00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.760
People decide: it’s a value, not a fact.

22
00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.170
Some harms come from how AI is used.

23
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.940
Deepfakes are AI-made photos, voices or

24
00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.680
videos that look real, like a fake

25
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.240
voice note from a teacher, or a picture

26
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.540
made to hurt a classmate.

27
00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.530
And face recognition can track people

28
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.510
through a market without them knowing.

29
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:24.790
So, AI ethics asks whether an AI is right

30
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.190
to use, not just whether it works.

31
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.340
It weighs who gains, who could be

32
00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.280
harmed, and who gets a say.

33
00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:34.790
Think of a school rule.

34
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.380
A good rule is fair, explained to

35
00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.900
everyone, and someone answers for it.

36
00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.500
A secret rule nobody can question

37
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.800
feels wrong, even when it works.

38
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.810
An AI that decides is a

39
00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.030
rule that runs itself.

40
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:51.880
Quick check!

41
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.480
Who should have a say in which

42
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.400
mistake the camera treats as worse?

43
00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.950
The people it affects, as well as

44
00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.450
those who make and use it.

45
00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.400
Every AI carries choices about

46
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.920
goals, data and trade-offs.

47
00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.690
Good news: choices can be

48
00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:10.950
questioned, and changed.

49
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.060
What can you do?

50
00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:16.430
If a photo, voice note or video shocks

51
00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.250
you, check before sharing: ask the

52
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.250
person in it, or find the source.

53
00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.570
Never make or forward a fake of a

54
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.450
real person, even as a joke.

55
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.460
Report fakes to an adult you trust.

56
00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.850
If someone wants to watch you with

57
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:34.010
AI, ask the five questions.

58
00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.280
In the app, choose a class trip:

59
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.000
museum, farm or science centre.

60
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:42.900
Set how much cost, learning,

61
00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.380
travel and safety matter, and

62
00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.980
watch the best choice change.

63
00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.410
The maths stays the same;

64
00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.350
the values are yours.

65
00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:53.260
Your turn.

66
00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.170
Imagine the camera recognises

67
00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.710
every student correctly.

68
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.180
Does that settle whether your

69
00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.220
school should use it?

70
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.740
No: accuracy answers just

71
00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.380
one of five questions.

72
00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.090
Remember: ask all five.

73
00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.070
An AI’s values are people’s

74
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.850
choices, so they can be questioned.

75
00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.680
And check fakes before you share.

76
00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:19.970
Try it yourself: hold a short

77
00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.610
debate at home or in class.

78
00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.160
Should our school use face

79
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.740
recognition for attendance?

80
00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.620
Both sides use the five questions.

81
00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.240
Then vote, and say what

82
00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.140
would change your mind.
